id: pm-gh1767
title: "GH-1767: Windows nightly history append test asserts a POSIX name-length errno"
description: "Nightly Validation run 45021851394 (windows-latest, Node 24, shard 3/4) failed on both attempts in tests/unit/sdk/history/reseed-append.spec.ts, case passes other creation failures through. The fixture creates a stream under a 300-character file name and asserts the errno ENAMETOOLONG. The Windows runner reports ENOENT for the same over-long name. The product contract under test is unchanged and correct: appendRecordToVerifiedStream propagates a non-collision creation failure unchanged. Only the expectation is platform-specific. This is the same class as pm-v3umtp (GH-1112)."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: ci,"gh:1767",nightly,tests,windows
created_at: "2026-11-22T18:43:04.907Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-22T21:04:43.533Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-22T21:04:41.260Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-22T21:04:41.260Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: "The case asserts that the propagated error carries the same code the filesystem reports for a direct exclusive create of the same path, with no errno literal; The case still proves a non-collision creation failure is not converted into a stream_changed refusal; The spec passes on Linux locally and the Windows nightly leg is green on the next scheduled run"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "The over-long name case compares the propagated error with the error a direct hard link to the same path reports, instead of the literal ENAMETOOLONG. Product code is unchanged."
expected_result: The spec passes on Linux and on the Windows Node 24 nightly leg without an errno literal
actual_result: 6 cases pass locally on Linux and dispatched Nightly Validation run 45067374000 on the fix branch passed all four Windows Node 24 shards
